{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_464516511c0919624e784e1287d95cab321c0ff3b445638529795cef84d4a7c6"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Each FileRecord tracks candidates, findings, an append-only analysisHistory, gitInfo, a lifecycle status (pending/processing/analyzed/error), and a lockedByRunId field used for atomic file claiming."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b6bed49895eecebc40b35a02a6ad4fc03946a9346b3a4d1fc1919a1ddbba76ec"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Only the name of the environment variable holding the model key is stored, never the key value itself; setup-state evidence likewise contains no credential values."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c1cb44e3925745ed552930bc70b4e219fd30ee62dabc58da7de0d9bf2bfb1b0a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"On-disk state is append-only: re-scans merge new candidates, re-processing appends to analysisHistory and merges findings, and revalidation annotates findings with verdicts without overwriting or deleting anything."}],"claim_ids":["clm_464516511c0919624e784e1287d95cab321c0ff3b445638529795cef84d4a7c6","clm_b6bed49895eecebc40b35a02a6ad4fc03946a9346b3a4d1fc1919a1ddbba76ec","clm_c1cb44e3925745ed552930bc70b4e219fd30ee62dabc58da7de0d9bf2bfb1b0a"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:30:26Z","created_by_operation":"op_25e0ec2c3a2e461b8e37bc1eef5a8fa8","id":"pg_09b5e53d52bc5e9495a0978f510b48d6","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/vercel-labs-deepsec-docs-data-layout-md-23a69227e338-978f510b48d6.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_3eab186a3a045b25a3505f1bdfd3ed8d"],"title":"vercel-labs/deepsec/docs/data-layout.md @ 23a69227e338","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:30:26Z","updated_by_operation":"op_25e0ec2c3a2e461b8e37bc1eef5a8fa8"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_b1249a365f93e8b24fc9c9eb9018cf0fec5f9eec118efbabafb3169fab884ae6"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"deepsec targets teams wanting deep, long-running vulnerability review of large existing codebases, with per-finding triage (~1 cent per finding) and revalidation priced comparably to the AI process stage."}],"claim_ids":["clm_b1249a365f93e8b24fc9c9eb9018cf0fec5f9eec118efbabafb3169fab884ae6"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:30:26Z","created_by_operation":"op_25e0ec2c3a2e461b8e37bc1eef5a8fa8","id":"pg_50ebabea3481558fba1eca594d2ff33a","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/vercel-labs-deepsec-docs-faq-md-23a69227e338-ca594d2ff33a.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_e0c09dde63205b8cbe40769641c6669a"],"title":"vercel-labs/deepsec/docs/faq.md @ 23a69227e338","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:30:26Z","updated_by_operation":"op_25e0ec2c3a2e461b8e37bc1eef5a8fa8"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_868d5db5ede5f73973baeac3c2fe9c0c8e2f0710ef309b7606f0f58b6ae7e8ff"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The architecture doc describes five plugin extension points in packages/core/src/plugin.ts: matchers, notifiers, and agents are additive, while ownership, people, and executor are single-slot with last-write-wins ordering."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9805870812e23e8c45bc01b85f098cb82d63934be157bd09d42560b814462a54"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Configuration lives in deepsec.config.ts (or .mjs/.js/.cjs) resolved from the current directory walking upward, declaring projects, plugins, matcher filters, default agent/model/thinking level, AI route, and dataDir."}],"claim_ids":["clm_868d5db5ede5f73973baeac3c2fe9c0c8e2f0710ef309b7606f0f58b6ae7e8ff","clm_9805870812e23e8c45bc01b85f098cb82d63934be157bd09d42560b814462a54"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:30:26Z","created_by_operation":"op_25e0ec2c3a2e461b8e37bc1eef5a8fa8","id":"pg_885a018dc9c65395a924e991ad944f91","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/vercel-labs-deepsec-docs-configuration-md-23a69227e338-e991ad944f91.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_39098c834c805138a3e18506b459dbf8"],"title":"vercel-labs/deepsec/docs/configuration.md @ 23a69227e338","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:30:26Z","updated_by_operation":"op_25e0ec2c3a2e461b8e37bc1eef5a8fa8"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:30:27Z","created_by_operation":"op_25e0ec2c3a2e461b8e37bc1eef5a8fa8","id":"pg_a4dfb1a252e251df89fea7293b996feb","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/vercel-labs-deepsec-skill-md-23a69227e338-a7293b996feb.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_b3a398bbbbed5b649034ce6e5e54c7aa"],"title":"vercel-labs/deepsec/SKILL.md @ 23a69227e338","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:30:27Z","updated_by_operation":"op_25e0ec2c3a2e461b8e37bc1eef5a8fa8"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_41663151cac87722586eb3112a3d9ca5d0244b2c5ce391fef28f9e27db391c62"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Because it uses top models at maximum thinking levels by default, scans of large codebases can cost thousands to tens of thousands of dollars, per the README's own cost warning."},{"claim_ids":["clm_4515bc54b8dea6324ec52352965a33d705d16f5b71fc42048f809b5d9dcbd3be"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The CLI exposes subcommands including scan, process, process --diff, triage, revalidate, enrich, report, export, metrics, status, and sandbox for running any command on Vercel Sandbox microVMs."},{"claim_ids":["clm_5351b712cea0ec0447ec8a87642522e69f09ec3ab43f435e88448376e24c5907"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"deepsec is an agent-powered vulnerability scanner that runs in the user's own infrastructure and is optimized for on-demand review of all code in large existing repositories."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9f355c8aff5522ff4e5fff4d92c2cdf6af4521e831cb6e1ae00c01db6135e1ae"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Large monorepos can optionally fan work across Vercel Sandbox microVMs; the local working tree is tarballed and uploaded (excluding .git), and model credentials stay host-side and are injected only at the egress host."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b1249a365f93e8b24fc9c9eb9018cf0fec5f9eec118efbabafb3169fab884ae6"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"deepsec targets teams wanting deep, long-running vulnerability review of large existing codebases, with per-finding triage (~1 cent per finding) and revalidation priced comparably to the AI process stage."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b2dfed48c617a9f5d12e5edd6b4643f2bcadeb989857841d6c018705cfcd7d0d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The security model treats deepsec like a coding agent with full shell access on its host environment; in sandbox mode, agent API keys are injected outside the sandbox and worker egress is limited to coding-agent hosts."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b37ec0fefb68564ecfa35c738009ab786ebd3dad642e86daf6f01dc594b706e8"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"By default model calls route through Vercel AI Gateway; users can instead bring their own OpenAI, Anthropic, or custom HTTPS provider key via --model-auth direct with --ai-provider and --ai-api-key-env."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b6bed49895eecebc40b35a02a6ad4fc03946a9346b3a4d1fc1919a1ddbba76ec"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Only the name of the environment variable holding the model key is stored, never the key value itself; setup-state evidence likewise contains no credential values."},{"claim_ids":["clm_cf77ee141d897b14cc35dd32e20cbd72396bd21915c0650cb9c4a8b573b60d40"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"For large codebases, work fans out across worker machines in parallel, and interrupted or errored runs can be re-run to resume, skipping already-analyzed files."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d1e35c69c040e76a282f80e6fb2785a1dc796ff0e0cafbf8609435a4aaa46688"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README warns of prompt-injection risk from external dependencies or vendored code even though the tool is designed to run on trusted source code."}],"claim_ids":["clm_41663151cac87722586eb3112a3d9ca5d0244b2c5ce391fef28f9e27db391c62","clm_4515bc54b8dea6324ec52352965a33d705d16f5b71fc42048f809b5d9dcbd3be","clm_5351b712cea0ec0447ec8a87642522e69f09ec3ab43f435e88448376e24c5907","clm_9f355c8aff5522ff4e5fff4d92c2cdf6af4521e831cb6e1ae00c01db6135e1ae","clm_b1249a365f93e8b24fc9c9eb9018cf0fec5f9eec118efbabafb3169fab884ae6","clm_b2dfed48c617a9f5d12e5edd6b4643f2bcadeb989857841d6c018705cfcd7d0d","clm_b37ec0fefb68564ecfa35c738009ab786ebd3dad642e86daf6f01dc594b706e8","clm_b6bed49895eecebc40b35a02a6ad4fc03946a9346b3a4d1fc1919a1ddbba76ec","clm_cf77ee141d897b14cc35dd32e20cbd72396bd21915c0650cb9c4a8b573b60d40","clm_d1e35c69c040e76a282f80e6fb2785a1dc796ff0e0cafbf8609435a4aaa46688"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:30:27Z","created_by_operation":"op_25e0ec2c3a2e461b8e37bc1eef5a8fa8","id":"pg_c4d59b694483528392b7315a1e6bd3a3","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/vercel-labs-deepsec-readme-md-23a69227e338-315a1e6bd3a3.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_ad7fe86ac0ca5d07be8665481b82df3a"],"title":"vercel-labs/deepsec/README.md @ 23a69227e338","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:30:27Z","updated_by_operation":"op_25e0ec2c3a2e461b8e37bc1eef5a8fa8"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_0cd68a7deeb0d5589eca6e9ef4c41a8e2a0198956fe916baf77a719274b74867"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The scan stage globs the project root, applies regex matchers to every matched file, and writes candidate matches into per-file FileRecords without any AI usage."},{"claim_ids":["clm_10c58a31819b721241fcc455430122a92831b302f6f55b8013bba0f8ecb9433e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Three agent backends are supported for process: codex (default, via @openai/codex-sdk), claude (via @anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk), and pi (via @earendil-works/pi-coding-agent), each with a documented default model."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3a44982f7830f0ddfd911d65ad3ee8c631bb4b12577bfd9a9ec30d95bf42a145"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The processor claims files atomically via lockedByRunId so multiple workers can run in parallel; concurrency and batch size flags control how many files are in flight."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6ee99b1a49d13d324d18b0292ba5406d2d903686c0e73c9e10d61f23ac85d278"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The setup coordinator uses a read-only agent to produce INFO.md and a structured surface inventory, evaluates scan coverage, generates data-only matcher specs validated for regex safety and slug collisions, and gates paid processing until coverage passes."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7777d76bbabddc6e65eb53320a473bee7ba741f52299d0e907174cbed290f855"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The process stage batches pending files, sends each batch to a configured AI agent backend with the system prompt and INFO.md, and parses JSON responses into findings stored on FileRecords."},{"claim_ids":["clm_868d5db5ede5f73973baeac3c2fe9c0c8e2f0710ef309b7606f0f58b6ae7e8ff"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The architecture doc describes five plugin extension points in packages/core/src/plugin.ts: matchers, notifiers, and agents are additive, while ownership, people, and executor are single-slot with last-write-wins ordering."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8ce0fb86a485d89e06007e71557f92699c8ad62d668c1ffa60ca24fbaf5ecc43"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The revalidate stage re-checks findings for false positives using git history and, per the docs, empirically reduces the false-positive rate by 50% or more on most repos."},{"claim_ids":["clm_bb5b194cf2f2df691e327770bca86bd9eaa7e2c15fe808a947e6585cdbac2611"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The unit of work is a source file rather than a finding, which the architecture doc says makes per-file atomic locking and idempotent merges natural."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c1cb44e3925745ed552930bc70b4e219fd30ee62dabc58da7de0d9bf2bfb1b0a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"On-disk state is append-only: re-scans merge new candidates, re-processing appends to analysisHistory and merges findings, and revalidation annotates findings with verdicts without overwriting or deleting anything."}],"claim_ids":["clm_0cd68a7deeb0d5589eca6e9ef4c41a8e2a0198956fe916baf77a719274b74867","clm_10c58a31819b721241fcc455430122a92831b302f6f55b8013bba0f8ecb9433e","clm_3a44982f7830f0ddfd911d65ad3ee8c631bb4b12577bfd9a9ec30d95bf42a145","clm_6ee99b1a49d13d324d18b0292ba5406d2d903686c0e73c9e10d61f23ac85d278","clm_7777d76bbabddc6e65eb53320a473bee7ba741f52299d0e907174cbed290f855","clm_868d5db5ede5f73973baeac3c2fe9c0c8e2f0710ef309b7606f0f58b6ae7e8ff","clm_8ce0fb86a485d89e06007e71557f92699c8ad62d668c1ffa60ca24fbaf5ecc43","clm_bb5b194cf2f2df691e327770bca86bd9eaa7e2c15fe808a947e6585cdbac2611","clm_c1cb44e3925745ed552930bc70b4e219fd30ee62dabc58da7de0d9bf2bfb1b0a"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:30:26Z","created_by_operation":"op_25e0ec2c3a2e461b8e37bc1eef5a8fa8","id":"pg_d875c52a104d5eb3a6aaa2580ae7fb5f","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/vercel-labs-deepsec-docs-architecture-md-23a69227e338-a2580ae7fb5f.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_5d9a5dc55ea55e04847a27bf7a0e0ba8"],"title":"vercel-labs/deepsec/docs/architecture.md @ 23a69227e338","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:30:26Z","updated_by_operation":"op_25e0ec2c3a2e461b8e37bc1eef5a8fa8"}
